***definitions***
- :Counter: tracks a numeric value that a :User: can increment, decrement, or reset.
  :Counter: has the following attributes:
  - Value - the current integer count. Starts at zero.
  - Label - an optional display name for the :Counter:.

***functional specifications***
- [id:CTR-1] :User: shall be able to increment a :Counter: by one.
- [id:CTR-2] :User: shall be able to decrement a :Counter: by one, but the value shall not go below zero.
- [id:CTR-3] :User: shall be able to reset a :Counter: to zero.

***acceptance tests***
- [covers:CTR-1] Given a :Counter: with Value 5, when :User: increments it, then Value becomes 6.
- [covers:CTR-2] Given a :Counter: with Value 0, when :User: decrements it, then Value remains 0.
- [covers:CTR-3] Given a :Counter: with Value 42, when :User: resets it, then Value becomes 0.
